 "notes": "95% credible upper limit on the scalar ULDM electron-mass coupling d_e from Fig. 14 (middle-top panel) of the NANOGrav 15-yr new-physics paper, extracted from the vector PDF (figs/uldm/scalar_uldm_constraints.pdf) and clipped to the plotted axis range 1e-24..1e-20 eV. The paper's Lagrangian Eq. (64), L = (phi/Lambda) d_e m_e ee with Lambda = M_Pl/sqrt(4pi), is identical to the Damour-Donoghue convention m_e -> m_e(1 + d_me kappa phi), so the paper's d_e is the canonical d_me with no conversion. The de panel shows a single red curve (correlated-regime analysis); this is the paper's headline limit for this coupling, which the text singles out (with d_mu) as its strongest constraint relative to laboratory bounds. Assumes ULDM is all of the local DM, rho_phi = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 (Table 1); paper notes limits weaken as sqrt(f_phi) for a subcomponent. The paper also bounds d_gamma, d_g, d_mhat, d_mu, g_B and g_B-L in Figs. 14-15.",
